<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{.Title}}</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<style>{{.CSS}}</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="top">
  <h1>{{.Title}}</h1>
  <div class="meta">
    generated <b>{{.Report.Generated.Format "2006-01-02 15:04 UTC"}}</b>
    · <b>{{.Report.Overview.TotalHosts}}</b> hosts
    · <b>{{commaInt .Report.Overview.TotalRecords}}</b> records
    · <b>{{.Report.Overview.TotalModules}}</b> modules
    · <b>{{.Report.Overview.TotalSiteClasses}}</b> site_classes
    {{if .Report.SkippedLines}}· <b style="color:var(--warn)">{{.Report.SkippedLines}}</b> malformed lines skipped{{end}}
    {{if .Report.AgentVersion}}· agent <b>{{.Report.AgentVersion}}</b>{{end}}
  </div>
  {{if .Report.Overview.DegradedHosts}}
  <div class="banner-warn">
    ⚠ coverage degraded on <b>{{len .Report.Overview.DegradedHosts}}</b> host(s): no package manager detected —
    the provenance gate (<code>non_package_path</code> / <code>package_file_tampered</code>) did NOT run on them, so
    absence of findings is <b>not</b> proof of clean. Treat these as <b>higher</b> priority for manual review + EDR pairing, not lower (ADR-0017).
    <details><summary>affected hosts</summary>
      <ul>{{range .Report.Overview.DegradedHosts}}<li>{{.Host}} <span class="muted">(os_id={{if .OSID}}{{.OSID}}{{else}}&lt;unknown&gt;{{end}})</span></li>{{end}}</ul>
    </details>
  </div>
  {{end}}
  {{if .Report.LFATriageOnly}}
  <div class="banner-warn">
    ⚠ <b>LFA triage-only</b>: no <code>(os_id, tag_set)</code> cohort reaches the peer-floor ({{.Report.PeerFloor}});
    {{.Report.SuppressedPeerGroups}} cohort(s) below it. Cross-host rarity (Q1/Q3 counts) has <b>no comparand</b> here —
    trust the population-independent path (<b>Q7</b>, <b>Q1 Actionable</b>, Tier-B). "0 Actionable" is <b>not</b> "clean" (ADR-0017).
  </div>
  {{end}}
</header>

<nav class="tabs">
  <button data-tab="q7">Q7 · implant roll-call</button>
  <button data-tab="overview">Overview</button>
  <button data-tab="q1">Q1 · LFA singletons</button>
  <button data-tab="q10">Q10 · host coverage</button>
  <button data-tab="q2">Q2 · per-locus singletons</button>
  <button data-tab="q3">Q3 · peer-group LFA</button>
  <button data-tab="q6">Q6 · worm pattern</button>
  <button data-tab="q8">Q8 · mtime concentration</button>
  <button data-tab="q9">Q9 · exec in /tmp</button>
  <button data-tab="q11">Q11 · orphan outside /tmp</button>
  <button data-tab="q12">Q12 · campaign clusters</button>
</nav>

<main>

  {{/* ========== Overview ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="overview">
    <h2>Fleet overview</h2>
    <p class="lede">High-level shape of the dataset. Use this to spot fleet-level anomalies (sudden mtime spike, signal explosion, OS imbalance) before drilling into the per-query tabs.</p>

    <div class="checklist">
      <b>Triage order</b> (population-independent first):
      <ol>
        <li><b>Q10</b> — confirm no host has module gaps (silent agent failure reads as "clean").</li>
        <li><b>Q7</b> — work the rule roll-call top-down (severity-sorted; critical first).</li>
        <li><b>Q1 → Actionable</b> — singletons with a structural tell, when no Q7 rule matched.</li>
        <li><b>Q8 / Q9 / Q11</b> — temporal bursts, armed-in-tmp, orphan payloads outside tmp.</li>
        <li><b>Q6 / Q12</b> — cross-host worm / campaign clustering.</li>
        <li><b>Q1 → Informational, Q2, Q3</b> — fleet-rarity context (degrades on small/peerless fleets — see banner).</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><div class="k">Hosts</div><div class="v">{{.Report.Overview.TotalHosts}}</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="k">Records</div><div class="v">{{commaInt .Report.Overview.TotalRecords}}</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="k">Modules</div><div class="v">{{.Report.Overview.TotalModules}}</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="k">Site_classes</div><div class="v">{{.Report.Overview.TotalSiteClasses}}</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="k">Q1 singletons</div><div class="v">{{len .Report.Q1Singletons}}</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="k">Q7 roll-call</div><div class="v" style="color:var(--tail)">{{len .Report.Q7ImplantRollCall}}</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="k">orphan+tmp (in Q7)</div><div class="v" style="color:var(--tail)">{{.Report.Overview.OrphanTmpCount}}</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="k">Q8 mtime spikes</div><div class="v">{{len .Report.Q8MtimeConcentration}}</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="k">Q11 orphan outside /tmp</div><div class="v" style="color:var(--tail)">{{len .Report.Q11OrphanOutsideTmp}}</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="k">MITRE techniques</div><div class="v">{{.Report.MITRECoverage.SurfacingTechniques}}/{{.Report.MITRECoverage.TotalTechniques}}<span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.7em"> surfacing</span></div></div>
    </div>

    <h2>LFA stacking histogram</h2>
    <p class="hint">Number of distinct <code>(module, content_norm_sha256)</code> groups that appear on N hosts. The singletons bucket is where attacker artefacts live; the right tail is the package-managed baseline.</p>
    <div class="hist">
      {{$max := histMax .Report.HistogramBuckets}}
      {{range .Report.HistogramBuckets}}
        <div class="bar{{if .IsTail}} tail{{end}}">
          <div class="bar-fill" style="height:{{histPct .Count $max}}px"></div>
          <div class="val">{{commaInt .Count}}</div>
          <div class="lbl">{{.Label}}</div>
        </div>
      {{end}}
    </div>

    <h2>Modules</h2>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-modules">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>module</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">records</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">hosts</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Overview.ByModule}}
          <tr><td>{{.Name}}</td><td class="num">{{commaInt .Records}}</td><td class="num">{{.Hosts}}</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Site classes</h2>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-siteclasses">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>site_class</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">records</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">hosts</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Overview.BySiteClass}}
          <tr><td>{{.Name}}</td><td class="num">{{commaInt .Records}}</td><td class="num">{{.Hosts}}</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>OS distribution</h2>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-os">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>os_id</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">hosts</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">records</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Overview.ByOSID}}
          <tr><td>{{.Name}}</td><td class="num">{{.Hosts}}</td><td class="num">{{commaInt .Records}}</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>MITRE ATT&amp;CK coverage</h2>
    <p class="hint">Techniques declared in <code>matrix.yaml</code> cross-referenced with live records. <b>surfacing</b> = at least one record carries the technique ID. <b>dormant_coverage_gap</b> = a covering module is active in the dataset but no record carries this technique (the operationally interesting case — review module MITRE tagging or the fleet sample). <b>dormant_module_silent</b> = no covering module emitted any record fleet-wide, so the site_class does not apply to this fleet shape (e.g. <code>grub</code>/<code>xdg</code> in container fleets).</p>
    {{if eq .Report.MITRECoverage.TotalTechniques 0}}
    <p class="hint"><em>matrix.yaml unavailable -- panel suppressed.</em></p>
    {{else}}
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-mitre">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>technique</th>
          <th>status</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">records</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">hosts</th>
          <th>site_classes</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.MITRECoverage.Rows}}
          <tr>
            <td><code>{{.TechniqueID}}</code></td>
            <td>{{if eq .Status "surfacing"}}<b>{{.Status}}</b>{{else if eq .Status "dormant_coverage_gap"}}<span style="color:var(--tail)">{{.Status}}</span>{{else}}<span style="color:var(--muted)">{{.Status}}</span>{{end}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.Records}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.Hosts}}</td>
            <td>{{range $i, $s := .SiteClasses}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}<code>{{$s}}</code>{{end}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {{end}}

    <h2>Signal distribution (fleet-wide)</h2>
    <p class="hint">Signals fired least often are the most analytically interesting (rare events). Bars represent host count.</p>
    {{$sigMax := signalMax .Report.Overview.BySignal}}
    <div class="bars">
      {{range .Report.Overview.BySignal}}
        <div class="row">
          <span class="name">{{.Name}}</span>
          <span class="bar"><span class="fill" style="width:{{signalPct .Hosts $sigMax}}%"></span></span>
          <span class="n">{{.Hosts}} / {{commaInt .Records}}</span>
        </div>
      {{end}}
    </div>
    <details class="drilldown">
      <summary>Break down by (module, signal) — which collector fired each signal ({{len .Report.Q5SignalDistribution}} rows)</summary>
      <div class="tbl-wrap">
        <table class="sortable" id="t-q5">
          <thead><tr><th>module</th><th>signal</th><th>hosts</th><th>records</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
          {{range .Report.Q5SignalDistribution}}
            <tr><td>{{.Module}}</td><td class="mono">{{.Signal}}</td><td>{{.Hosts}}</td><td>{{commaInt .Records}}</td></tr>
          {{else}}
            <tr><td colspan="4" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no rows</td></tr>
          {{end}}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  {{/* ========== Q1 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q1">
    <h2>Q1 · Pure LFA singletons</h2>
    <p class="lede">Records whose <code>content_norm_sha256</code> appears on exactly one host in the fleet. This is the load-bearing query: an attacker who appends a malicious line to <code>/etc/crontab</code> on one host produces a digest no other host has, and it surfaces here.</p>
    <p class="hint"><b>ADR-0017 discriminator ladder.</b> Content-rarity only discriminates where a valid comparand population exists, and homogeneity is a property of a <code>(host, site_class)</code> pair, not of a host. So Q1 is split: <b>Actionable</b> rows carry a structural co-indicator (orphan/non-package/tmp/tamper/recent/…) and are real <em>regardless</em> of fleet size; <b>Informational</b> rows are bare content-singletons (<code>co=0</code>) — at N=1 every record is a singleton, so rarity alone is weak. The informational rows are <b>never suppressed</b>: triage them, and restore verdict-power with a sized peer cohort (Q3), a prior snapshot (diff mode), or EDR pairing.</p>

    {{$act := q1Actionable .Report.Q1Singletons}}
    <h3 class="grp-ok">Actionable — rung 1: structural co-indicator present ({{len $act}})</h3>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q1a">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q1a">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>co</th><th>module</th><th>site_class</th>
          <th>content_norm</th><th>sample_host</th>
          <th>sample_locus</th><th>sample_snippet</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range $act}}
          <tr>
            <td><b>{{.CoIndicators}}</b></td>
            <td>{{.Module}}</td><td>{{.SiteClass}}</td>
            <td class="hash">{{.ContentNorm}}</td>
            <td>{{.SampleHost}}</td>
            <td class="path">{{.SampleLocus}}</td>
            <td class="snippet">{{.SampleSnippet}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="7" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no rung-1 rows — no singleton carries a structural co-indicator</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    {{$inf := q1Info .Report.Q1Singletons}}
    <h3 class="grp-info">Informational — rung 4: bare content-novelty, no structural tell ({{len $inf}})</h3>
    <p class="hint">Not a verdict and not suppressed. Sorted by <code>rec</code> (recent_{mtime,ctime} count) — a freshly-changed unique file is the likelier implant; recency never promotes to Actionable because on a freshly-imaged host it fires on almost everything. <code>disc=novelty-only</code> = provenance was structurally inapplicable (a webroot-class walk; no tell was ever possible). <code>disc=no-tell</code> = a structural tell could have fired and did not (genuinely unremarkable, or a backdated/owned-path implant on a peerless host — the irreducible boundary, ADR-0017).</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q1i">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q1i">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>rec</th><th>disc</th><th>module</th><th>site_class</th>
          <th>content_norm</th><th>sample_host</th>
          <th>sample_locus</th><th>sample_snippet</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range $inf}}
          <tr>
            <td>{{if .Recency}}{{.Recency}}{{else}}<span class="muted">0</span>{{end}}</td>
            <td><span class="muted">{{.Disc}}</span></td>
            <td>{{.Module}}</td><td>{{.SiteClass}}</td>
            <td class="hash">{{.ContentNorm}}</td>
            <td>{{.SampleHost}}</td>
            <td class="path">{{.SampleLocus}}</td>
            <td class="snippet">{{.SampleSnippet}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="8" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no bare singletons</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* ========== Q2 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q2">
    <h2>Q2 · Per-locus LFA singletons</h2>
    <p class="lede">Like Q1 but also groups by <code>locus</code>. Catches the case where the same content is universal but appears at an unusual path on one host (renamed copy, look-alike location).</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q2">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q2">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>module</th><th>site_class</th><th>locus</th>
          <th>content_norm</th><th>sample_host</th><th>sample_snippet</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Q2LocusSingletons}}
          <tr>
            <td>{{.Module}}</td><td>{{.SiteClass}}</td>
            <td class="path">{{.Locus}}</td>
            <td class="hash">{{.ContentNorm}}</td>
            <td>{{.SampleHost}}</td>
            <td class="snippet">{{.SampleSnippet}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="6" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no per-locus singletons</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* ========== Q3 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q3">
    <h2>Q3 · Peer-group LFA by (os_id, tags)</h2>
    <p class="lede">Singletons inside their own <code>(os_id, tag_set)</code> cohort. Fixes Q1's fragmentation: a Debian-only baseline does not look like a singleton in a mixed Debian/RHEL fleet.</p>
    <p class="hint">peer-floor = <b>{{.Report.PeerFloor}}</b> · <b>{{.Report.QualifyingPeerGroups}}</b> cohort(s) qualify · <b>{{.Report.SuppressedPeerGroups}}</b> suppressed below the floor.</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q3">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q3">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>os_id</th><th>module</th><th>site_class</th>
          <th>content_norm</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">peer_size</th>
          <th>sample_host</th>
          <th>sample_locus</th>
          <th>sample_snippet</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Q3PeerGroupSingletons}}
          <tr>
            <td>{{.OSID}}</td><td>{{.Module}}</td><td>{{.SiteClass}}</td>
            <td class="hash">{{.ContentNorm}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.PeerSize}}</td>
            <td>{{.SampleHost}}</td>
            <td class="path">{{.SampleLocus}}</td>
            <td class="snippet">{{.SampleSnippet}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          {{if eq .Report.QualifyingPeerGroups 0}}
          <tr><td colspan="8" style="text-align:center;color:var(--warn)">SUPPRESSED — all {{.Report.SuppressedPeerGroups}} cohort(s) are below peer-floor {{.Report.PeerFloor}}. This is NOT "clean": lower <code>--peer-floor</code> or add ≥{{.Report.PeerFloor}} role replicas per cohort.</td></tr>
          {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="8" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">cohorts qualify but carry no singleton</td></tr>
          {{end}}
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* Q4 (orphan+tmp fingerprint) folded into Q7 — strict subset of the
       payload_under_tmp_via_persistence detection. Count is an Overview
       badge; the orphan view is the Q9 is_orphan column. Q5 (signal
       distribution) folded into the Overview signal-bars drill-down. */}}

  {{/* ========== Q6 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q6">
    <h2>Q6 · Cross-host exec_target stacking (worm pattern)</h2>
    <p class="lede">Records on different hosts whose persistence text differs but whose <code>exec_target_sha256</code> matches: identical <strong>non-package</strong> payload, polymorphic persistence. Packaged binaries shared fleet-wide are excluded (they are baseline, not worms); on large fleets a <code>10%-of-hosts</code> ceiling further trims baseline, and singletons stay Q1 turf.</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q6">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q6">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>exec_target_sha256</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">hosts</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">records</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">modules</th>
          <th>sample_target</th>
          <th>spread</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Q6ExecTargetStacking}}
          <tr>
            <td class="hash">{{.ExecTargetSHA256}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.Hosts}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{commaInt .Records}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.Modules}}</td>
            <td class="target">{{.SampleTarget}}</td>
            <td class="sig-list">{{range .SpreadModules}}<span class="sig">{{.}}</span>{{end}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="6" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no cross-host worm pattern detected</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* ========== Q7 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q7">
    <h2>Q7 · Implant roll-call (cross-cutting union)</h2>
    <p class="lede">The single highest-signal query in the cookbook. One row per record that matches <em>any</em> of the canonical implant patterns: orphan+tmp, sudoers backdoors, uid=0 backdoors, kmod install replacements, profile/motd curl|wget content, sysv scripts referencing /tmp. The clauses are deliberately disjoint — every implant lands on exactly one row.</p>
    <div class="sev-summary">
      <span class="item"><span class="sev critical">critical</span> <span class="count">{{index .Report.Overview.SeverityCounts "critical"}}</span></span>
      <span class="item"><span class="sev high">high</span> <span class="count">{{index .Report.Overview.SeverityCounts "high"}}</span></span>
      <span class="item"><span class="sev medium">medium</span> <span class="count">{{index .Report.Overview.SeverityCounts "medium"}}</span></span>
      <span class="item"><span class="sev low">low</span> <span class="count">{{index .Report.Overview.SeverityCounts "low"}}</span></span>
      <span class="item"><span class="sev info">info</span> <span class="count">{{index .Report.Overview.SeverityCounts "info"}}</span></span>
    </div>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q7">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q7">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>severity</th>
          <th>host</th><th>module</th><th>site_class</th>
          <th>locus</th><th>exec_target</th><th>matched_detections</th><th>triage_signals</th><th>snippet</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Q7ImplantRollCall}}
          <tr>
            <td>{{with .MaxSeverity}}<span class="sev {{.}}">{{.}}</span>{{else}}<span class="sev unspec">—</span>{{end}}</td>
            <td>{{.Host}}</td><td>{{.Module}}</td><td>{{.SiteClass}}</td>
            <td class="path">{{.Locus}}</td>
            <td class="target">{{.ExecTarget}}</td>
            <td class="sig-list">{{range .MatchedDetections}}<span class="sig warn">{{.}}</span>{{end}}</td>
            <td class="sig-list">{{range .TriageSignals}}<span class="sig{{if signalIsWarn .}} warn{{end}}">{{.}}</span>{{end}}</td>
            <td class="snippet">{{.Snippet}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="9" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no implant patterns detected — clean fleet</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* ========== Q8 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q8">
    <h2>Q8 · Recent-mtime concentration per host × module</h2>
    <p class="lede">Hosts × modules where five or more persistence records carry <code class="sig">recent_mtime_7d</code>. Spikes are either a config-management push (legitimate, correlatable with the orchestration tool's change log) or a post-compromise sweep (attacker hardening persistence after initial access). Zero rows on a quiet fleet is the expected state.</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q8">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q8">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>host</th><th>module</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">recent_records</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">recent_loci</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Q8MtimeConcentration}}
          <tr>
            <td>{{.Host}}</td><td>{{.Module}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.RecentRecords}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.RecentLoci}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="4" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no concentrated mtime activity in the last 7 days</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* ========== Q9 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q9">
    <h2>Q9 · Exec targets under /tmp, /var/tmp, /dev/shm, /run/shm</h2>
    <p class="lede">Q4 requires <em>both</em> orphan and interpreter_in_tmp; this query is the open half. Records whose <code>exec_target</code> lives in a tmp-class directory, orphan or not. The <code>is_orphan</code> column tells the analyst whether the payload is currently armed (false = armed and on disk; true = dormant or post-execution). Q9 set minus Q4 = "currently armed implants".</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q9">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q9">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>host</th><th>module</th><th>site_class</th>
          <th>locus</th><th>exec_target</th>
          <th>is_orphan</th><th>snippet</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Q9ExecInTmp}}
          <tr>
            <td>{{.Host}}</td><td>{{.Module}}</td><td>{{.SiteClass}}</td>
            <td class="path">{{.Locus}}</td>
            <td class="target">{{.ExecTarget}}</td>
            <td>{{if .IsOrphan}}yes{{else}}no{{end}}</td>
            <td class="snippet">{{.Snippet}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="7" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no exec targets under tmp-class directories</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* ========== Q10 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q10">
    <h2>Q10 · Per-host collection health and coverage outliers</h2>
    <p class="lede"><b>Run this first.</b> For each host: records, distinct modules, distinct site_classes, and <b>gap_modules</b> — modules the rest of the fleet emits (fleet median &gt; 0) but this host emitted ZERO records for. A non-empty gap_modules is a silent agent failure / image gap that would otherwise read as "clean" across every other tab. Hosts with gaps are sorted to the top.</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q10">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q10">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>host</th><th>os_id</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">records</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">modules</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">site_classes</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">recent_records</th>
          <th>gap_modules</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Q10HostCoverage}}
          <tr>
            <td>{{.Host}}</td><td>{{.OSID}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{commaInt .Records}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.Modules}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.SiteClasses}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.RecentRecords}}</td>
            <td class="sig-list">{{if .GapModules}}{{range .GapModules}}<span class="sig warn">{{.}}</span>{{end}}{{else}}<span class="muted">—</span>{{end}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="7" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no host records — dataset is empty</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* ========== Q11 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q11">
    <h2>Q11 · Orphan exec_target OUTSIDE tmp-class directories</h2>
    <p class="lede">The implant pattern Q4 and Q9 miss entirely: the attacker drops the payload under a long-lived but unmanaged path (<code>/opt/</code>, <code>/var/lib/</code>, <code>/srv/</code>, <code>/usr/local/</code>) and wires persistence to it. The payload is not in <code>/tmp</code> so <code>interpreter_in_tmp</code> does not fire; the payload exists on disk so <code>exec_target_orphan</code> does not fire either. The only signal that catches it is <code>non_package_path</code> from the provenance resolver. LFA-sorted (hosts ascending): singletons are the highest-precision hits.</p>
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows…" data-target="#t-q11">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q11">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>exec_target</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">hosts</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">records</th>
          <th>module</th>
          <th>site_class</th>
          <th>sample_host</th>
          <th>sample_locus</th>
          <th>sample_snippet</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Q11OrphanOutsideTmp}}
          <tr>
            <td><code>{{.ExecTarget}}</code></td>
            <td class="num">{{.Hosts}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.Records}}</td>
            <td>{{.Module}}</td>
            <td>{{.SiteClass}}</td>
            <td>{{.SampleHost}}</td>
            <td class="path">{{.SampleLocus}}</td>
            <td class="snippet">{{.SampleSnippet}}</td>
          </tr>
        {{else}}
          <tr><td colspan="8" style="text-align:center;color:var(--fg-mute)">no orphan exec_targets outside /tmp class detected</td></tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* ========== Q12 ========== */}}
  <section class="pane" data-pane="q12">
    <h2>Q12 · Campaign basename clusters</h2>
    <p class="lede">Same basename of <code>exec_target</code> (or <code>locus</code> when exec_target is empty) appearing in two or more modules across two or more hosts, where at least one arm carries a persistence-anomaly signal (<code>non_package_path</code> / <code>exec_target_orphan</code> / <code>interpreter_in_tmp</code>). Surfaces multi-arm campaigns whose individual arms each look like Q1 singletons in their own module (the v0.2.0 deploy-sync pattern); coincidental package baseline shared fleet-wide is excluded. Sorted ascending by host count.</p>
    <p class="hint">Expect FPs from vendor baselines shipping the same name in <code>systemd.unit</code> and <code>sysv.init</code> (nginx, redis-server, prometheus, cron). Triage from the top -- rare cross-module pairs are the interesting ones.</p>
    {{if .Report.Q12BasenameClustering}}
    <input class="search" type="search" placeholder="filter rows..." data-target="#t-q12">
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="sortable" id="t-q12">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>basename</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">hosts</th>
          <th data-sort-type="num">records</th>
          <th>modules</th>
          <th>sample_host</th>
          <th>sample_exec_target / locus</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {{range .Report.Q12BasenameClustering}}
          <tr>
            <td><code>{{.Basename}}</code></td>
            <td class="num">{{.Hosts}}</td>
            <td class="num">{{.Records}}</td>
            <td>{{range $i, $m := .Modules}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}<code>{{$m}}</code>{{end}}</td>
            <td>{{.SampleHost}}</td>
            <td><code>{{if .SampleExecTarget}}{{.SampleExecTarget}}{{else}}(locus) {{.SampleLocus}}{{end}}</code></td>
          </tr>
        {{end}}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {{else}}
    <p class="hint">No rows. Either the fleet contains no cross-module basename overlaps, or every overlap landed on a single host.</p>
    {{end}}
  </section>


</main>

<script>{{ .JS }}</script>
</body>
</html>
